Handwritten Digit Recognition using CNN

A Convolutional Neural Network trained on the MNIST dataset (60,000 training images, 10,000 test images) to classify handwritten digits (0–9), with support for predicting on your own handwritten digit photos.

Stack: TensorFlow / Keras, NumPy, Matplotlib, OpenCV, scikit-learn

Project Structure
mnist_cnn_project/
├── train_model.py      # Builds, trains, evaluates, and saves the CNN
├── predict.py           # Loads the saved model and predicts on new images
├── requirements.txt
├── outputs/              # Generated plots (created automatically)
└── mnist_cnn_model.keras # Saved model (created after training)
